title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Configure a step › Payer rules
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: Rule steps (submission window, backdating, no-authorization exemption, continued stay, units and duration, clinical criteria, submission method, appeal deadline, peer-to-peer) point at a rule in the payer's central library. The workflow holds only the pointer, so a change to the rule is seen by every workflow that uses it and no policy text is copied.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Select a rule step\nsuch as 'Submission window'"
screen rp "Rule picker for that group\nOne card per rule of that kind: its title, a chip Verified, Needs review, Unverified or Superseded,\nits source ('Demo sample rules, version 2026.3'), dates in force, version,\nthe services and request types it covers"
decision d1 "Does the payer have a rule of this kind?"
screen e1 "'Summit has no rule of this kind on file. With none chosen, the step cannot say what the payer requires and sends the case to manual review.'"
click c1 "Tick a rule"
process p1 "The step points at that rule\nSeeded rules are demo samples, so the chip says 'Unverified'"
decision d2 "Does the step point at a rule that was deleted?"
screen w1 "'A rule this step points at no longer exists in the library. Choose again, or the workflow cannot be published.'"
click c2 "Click 'Open in Rules & Instructions'"
process p2 "Leaves the builder for that rule's group (asks first if there are unsaved changes)"
screen adv "Advanced: 'If the rule is unverified'\n'Go on and show a warning' (default) or 'Send to manual review'"
process p3 "Unverified rules never read as certain\nA test run lists each rule it read with its chip"
process p4 "Checks warn: 'uses ... which is unverified'\nThis does not block publishing"
end e2 "The step points at the right rule and says what to do when it is unverified"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Rules & Instructions › Read the rules"
goto g2 "Continues in: Payers › Rules & Instructions › Mark a rule as verified"

s1 --> rp --> d1
d1 -->|No| e1 --> p4
d1 -->|Yes| c1 --> p1 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| w1 --> p4
d2 -->|No| p4
rp --> c2 --> p2 --> g1
rp --> adv --> p3 --> p4
p4 --> e2
p2 --> g2
